<div class="g-prose"><p>The Opinion tab supplies the document sections, counsel, judges and footnotes. A continuous 1px track and 2×12px position marker keep the rail visually light; links retain 24px targets and the thumb has a 26×28px invisible hitbox. Other tabs keep their list or history navigation without a document scrubber. The rail re-measures as content and fonts change. Reduced motion uses immediate movement.</p></div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="search">Search within the opinion</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>Activate the rail's search icon to widen that control from left to right into the reader search field. The field keeps the icon's origin; up to five matching excerpts, the result count and match navigation appear directly below after a query. Choosing an excerpt hides the excerpt rows and focuses that match in the opinion; the query, count and previous/next controls stay available. Focus or edit the field to reopen the excerpt rows. The query stays when closed. Results come from the opinion text, not the case index. A compact trigger remains available when the rail is absent; opening search from another tab returns to Opinion. Leaving Opinion closes the field without clearing its query.</p></div>
